  "guideDashboardTitle": "Your dashboard",
  "guideDashboardBody": "Everything opens here. The card at the top is what you have left; under it sits what came in and what went out this period, then your spending, budgets and goals.",
  "guideDashboardTip1": "Pull the screen down to refresh everything at once.",
  "guideDashboardTip2": "Tap the income or expenses card to jump to that list.",
  "guideDashboardTip3": "The rings and insights update the moment you record something.",
  "guideAddTitle": "Recording money",
  "guideAddBody": "The button in the middle of the bar is where everything starts. It opens a short menu: money out, money in, a debt, a budget or a savings goal.",
  "guideAddTip1": "Tap the centre button to record money in or out.",
  "guideAddTip2": "Hold it down to go straight to a new expense and skip the menu.",
  "guideAddTip3": "Always pick a category — that is what makes the charts and budgets work.",
  "guideCategoriesTitle": "Categories",
  "guideCategoriesBody": "Categories are how spending gets grouped. The ones that ship with the app cover most people, and you can rename them or add your own.",
  "guideCategoriesTip1": "Settings, then Manage categories, to change or add one.",
  "guideCategoriesTip2": "Anything left uncategorised lands in Other, so the charts stay honest.",
  "guideBudgetTitle": "Budgets",
  "guideBudgetBody": "A budget is a monthly ceiling for one category. The bar fills as you spend and turns as it gets close, so you find out before you have gone through it.",
  "guideBudgetTip1": "Start with two or three categories, not all of them at once.",
  "guideBudgetTip2": "Set the limit slightly above what you usually spend, then tighten it.",
  "guideBudgetTip3": "Leave budget alerts on and the app warns you as one runs low.",
  "guideSavingsTitle": "Savings goals",
  "guideSavingsBody": "Name what you are saving for, set a target and a date, and the app works out what you need to put aside each month to get there.",
  "guideSavingsTip1": "A named goal is easier to keep than a vague intention to save.",
  "guideSavingsTip2": "Several small goals get finished more often than one large one.",
  "guideLoansTitle": "Debts and loans",
  "guideLoansBody": "Record what you owe, what it costs and when the next payment falls due. Everything you are paying off sits in one list with the total left on it.",
  "guideLoansTip1": "Add the due date and payment reminders will chase it for you.",
  "guideLoansTip2": "A debt marked overdue shows in red on the dashboard until it is paid.",
  "guideReportsTitle": "Reports",
  "guideReportsBody": "The deeper view: income against expenses, spending by category, how your budgets held up, and what share of your income you kept.",
  "guideReportsTip1": "Switch between week, month and quarter at the top of the screen.",
  "guideReportsTip2": "Export or share a PDF — it comes out in your own language and direction.",
  "guideSettingsTitle": "Settings",
  "guideSettingsBody": "Language, currency, colours and alerts all live here, and none of them are locked in by setup — change any of them whenever you like.",
  "guideSettingsTip1": "Forty languages, and the whole layout mirrors for right-to-left ones.",
  "guideSettingsTip2": "Pick which alerts you want and the hours they may arrive.",
  "guideSettingsTip3": "Quiet hours hold everything back until the morning.",
  "guideHabitTitle": "Make it stick",
  "guideHabitBody": "The app is only as good as what you put into it. A minute a day beats an hour once a month, and after a fortnight the numbers start telling you something.",
  "guideHabitTip1": "Record what you spend as it happens, not at the end of the week.",
  "guideHabitTip2": "Glance at the dashboard once a day. Ten seconds is enough.",
  "guideHabitTip3": "This guide stays in Settings — come back to it whenever you like.",
